---
const { simple = false } = Astro.props;
---
{simple ? (
<figure class="authority-flow simple-flow" aria-label="Human authority flows through an agent to a verifying service">
  <figcaption>Target architecture · A permission travels. A service checks it.</figcaption>
  <ol class="authority-roles">
    <li><span class="category">01 / Human</span><h3>You authorize.</h3><p>One ticket. Up to $480. Once.</p><span class="mandate-token">Bounded mandate <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></li>
    <li><span class="category">02 / Agent</span><h3>Your agent acts.</h3><p>It carries your permission with the exact purchase request.</p><span class="mandate-token">Mandate + request <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></li>
    <li class="verifying-role"><span class="category">03 / Verifying service</span><h3>The service checks.</h3><p>The merchant or trusted gateway verifies the mandate and agent, then applies its policy before purchase.</p><span class="verification-boundary">Within the limits? Proceed.<br>Outside them? Reject.</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="flow-caption">The service enforces the boundary. The agent cannot widen your permission.</p>
</figure>
) : (
<figure class="authority-flow" aria-label="Human authority flows through an agent to a verifying service">
  <figcaption>Target architecture · Authority travels with the action</figcaption>
  <ol class="authority-roles">
    <li>
      <span class="category">01 / Human</span>
      <h3>Grant authority.</h3>
      <p>Approve a bounded action with a passkey on your personal device.</p>
      <span class="flow-handoff">Mandate and approval evidence →</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="category">02 / Agent</span>
      <h3>Act within it.</h3>
      <p>Run locally or remotely. Present the mandate and proof of the bound agent key.</p>
      <span class="flow-handoff">Exact action and agent proof →</span>
    </li>
    <li class="verifying-role">
      <span class="category">03 / Verifying service</span>
      <h3>Check before committing.</h3>
      <p>A merchant, payment service, API or trusted gateway checks authority at its enforcement boundary.</p>
      <span class="flow-handoff">Verify · Apply policy · Reserve use</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="flow-outcomes">
    <p><strong>Valid and permitted:</strong> commit the authorized action, then record its outcome.</p>
    <p><strong>Invalid, expired or already used:</strong> reject. Missing authority may require a new approval.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="flow-caption">Routine work stays within existing permission. Fresh approval is for selected consequential boundaries, not every tool call. Diagram shows roles, not a finalized wire protocol.</p>
</figure>
)}
